\description{
\strong{Player box score of one B.LEAGUE game: one row per (player, period category), both
teams.}

Endpoint: \verb{GET https://b-league.s3.amazonaws.com/web_json/v2_genius_contexts/\{schedule_key\}/\{latest\}.json}
(the v1 feed, or the game page's embed, when v2 does not hold the game).

Rows with \code{category} 1 (a player), one per \code{period_category} (1-4 quarters, 15 / 16
halves, 18 the whole game; overtime categories are unverified). \code{seconds_played} is
\code{play_time} in seconds (\code{DNP} = \code{NA}). The v2 feed sends \code{""} as a placeholder (not
0) in some cells; those are \code{NA} here. The efficiency definition differs by feed, the
advanced columns (\code{plus_minus}, \code{ast_to}, \code{efg}, \code{ts}, \code{usg}) exist from 2022-23 on
v2 only, and \code{dunks} / \code{ptpft} exist on v1 only.
